# Large frozen oracles: NOT in git, but pinned by oracle/MANIFEST.sha256.
# Regenerate with the commands in oracle/README.md, then verify against the
# manifest — that is what makes them oracles rather than just files.
*.dump
*.afb.0
*.fb1
# .roots1 is the CADO-format factor base bench reads via --cadofb. Ignored for
# the same reason as *.fb1: oracle/c147.roots1 is 29 MB and regenerates exactly
# from the 543-byte oracle/c147.job, which IS committed.
*.roots1
# Per-logI variants of the same thing: oracle/c194.roots1.m15 / .m16 are 197 MB
# each and regenerate from the 644-byte oracle/c194.job. The bare `*.roots1`
# glob does NOT match a suffixed name, so this line is load-bearing.
*.roots1.m*

# Captured survivor / cofactor populations. Same rule: manifest-pinned, not
# committed. gzip and tar do not delta-compress, so committing these would add
# their full size to every clone, permanently, for data that is reproducible.
*.txt.gz
*.tar.gz

# Build products
*.o
# MSVC objects and executable from bench/build_windows.bat. Untracked build
# products set the build stamp's -dirty flag (see the note further down), so
# one Windows build would otherwise brand every later build in the same
# checkout -- including a WSL/Linux one -- as dirty.
*.obj
bench/bench
bench/bench.exe
bench/bench_hip.exe
bench/bench_hip_boinc.exe
# Written by BOINC's client library at runtime when a HAVE_BOINC binary runs
# standalone (no real BOINC client/init_data.xml present).
bench/boinc_finish_called
bench/stderr.txt
bench/fbtest
bench/fbtest.exe
bench/fbgen
bench/fbgen.exe
bench/fbgen_gpu
bench/fbgen_gpu.exe
bench/fbgen_gpu_hip.exe
bench/sqgentest
bench/sqgentest.exe
bench/normscan
bench/normscan.exe
bench/dumpcmp
bench/dumpcmp.exe
bench/mkcofbatch
bench/mkcofbatch.exe
bench/ckpttest
bench/ckpttest.exe
bench/stoptest
bench/stoptest.exe
bench/slabtest
bench/slabtest.exe
# wintest.bat outputs (cross-platform byte-comparison harness)
bench/wintest.dat*
bench/wintest.out
bench/wintest.runlog
bench/.arch.stamp
bench/.boinc.stamp
bench/.link.stamp
bench/.git.stamp
bench/.defs.stamp
bench/.cflmax.stamp
bench/.bnlimbs.stamp
*.d

# All per-job working state lives under work/: poly, factor base, relations,
# msieve output. Reproducible from the RUNBOOK recipe, and a single relation
# file runs to several GB. One rule rather than a pattern per job name, so a
# new job directory cannot be committed by being named something unexpected.
/work/

# Root-finder scratch. Named NAME.tmp.PID and renamed on success, so a stray
# one is the residue of an interrupted makefb-side run, never an input.
*.tmp.[0-9]*

# Generated factor bases and job copies left in the build directory. These
# are reproducible from fbgen and would otherwise keep the tree permanently
# "dirty", which defeats the run log's build stamp (see bench/Makefile).
bench/fbase
bench/input.job
bench/*.m14
bench/*.m15
bench/*.m16
bench/fbase.m*

# Python bytecode from the analysis tools (relgeom.py and friends). Untracked
# files set the build stamp's -dirty flag, which is what makes the run log's
# commit field meaningful -- see bench/Makefile.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.dat
*.poly
*.log

